                <pb facs="0321" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg256"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">384.11/124: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-03T10:00:00+02:35">May 3, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 3—6:02 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>269. My 268.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d273-f1"/> With cooperation of British
                    Legation which provided two trucks in charge of Vice Consul Trapman the
                    following were safely removed to British Legation this morning: Mrs. Bergman and
                    two children, Mr. and Mrs. Hansen, two Swedish and two Norwegian nurses. Dr.
                    Stadin will probably follow later. Dr. Bergman states he prefers to remain at
                    hospital.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
